Wayfinder's TypeScript runtime does not know the QUERY verb that Laravel 13.35
added: Route::redirect() and Route::any() now register it, the generated route
files emit "query", and `bun run test:types` fails on the union below. Backport
of laravel/wayfinder#324 (issue #326), the stub hunk only.

Retire when: laravel/wayfinder >= 0.1.22

--- a/resources/js/wayfinder.ts
+++ b/resources/js/wayfinder.ts
@@ -9,7 +9,8 @@
         | QueryParams;
 };
 
-type Method = "get" | "post" | "put" | "delete" | "patch" | "head" | "options";
+type Method =
+    "get" | "post" | "put" | "delete" | "patch" | "head" | "options" | "query";
 type UrlDefaults = Record<string, unknown>;
 
 let urlDefaults: () => UrlDefaults = () => ({});
